# HillGPX environment — copy to .env or .env.local for local development.
# Both files are gitignored; never commit real values. A fresh clone needs
# none of this: the defaults baked into the app already point at the live
# Supabase project.

# --- Supabase (community backend) ---
# Only needed to point the app at a different Supabase project (a fork or a
# staging copy). The publishable key is public by design — row-level security
# limits it to inserting new rows and reading approved ones.
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://yourproject.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_KEY=sb_publishable_...

# --- Accounts ---
# Google sign-in. Create an OAuth client ID (type "Web application") in Google
# Cloud → APIs & Services → Credentials, with the site's JavaScript origin,
# then add the same client ID under Supabase → Authentication → Providers →
# Google. Leave empty to keep email sign-up only.
# VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# --- One-time MongoDB rescue (scripts/migrate_from_mongo.py) ---
# Service-role key from Supabase dashboard → Settings → API, and the Mongo
# connection the retired api/ stack used. Delete after a successful run.
# SUPABASE_URL=https://dzpgnebkyubeptitzjlj.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY=
# MONGO_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017
# MONGO_DB=hillgpx

# --- Data scripts (unchanged) ---
# See scripts/README.md — OneMap for ingest_hdb.py, Mapillary for
# fetch_photos.py, Groq/FreeLLM for describe_venues.py, Strava for
# import_gpx.py. None are needed to run the app.

# --- Google Health linking (src/lib/googleHealth.ts) ---
# No env vars and no server: the same VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID drives a GIS
# token client in the browser, which calls health.googleapis.com directly.
# Setup is all in Google Cloud: enable the Google Health API on the project
# that owns the sign-in OAuth client, and add the scopes
# googlehealth.activity_and_fitness.readonly and googlehealth.location.readonly
# to its OAuth consent screen (test users while it stays in Testing mode).

# --- Pages Function moderation (functions/api/moderate.js) ---
# OPENAI_API_KEY does NOT go here: the function never reads .env. Put it in
# .dev.vars for `wrangler pages dev`, or Cloudflare Pages → Settings →
# Variables and Secrets for production. The moderation endpoint is free.
